# sweep: --bare
# Logging works before any pack arrives, and a pack pushed later fills the tally.
wait-for No field pack yet
tap Start an outing
wait-for Name this place
type back garden
tap Save
wait-for back garden
expect 0 species, 0 birds
expect Type the first bird you see.
clean
shot nopack-outing
# With no pack the search asks only for the name.
tap Type a species
wait-for Type the species you see.
type wren
tap Find
wait-for Log “wren” by name
expect-missing No species in your packs matches
clean
shot nopack-log-by-name
tap Log “wren” by name
wait-for 1 species, 1 bird
# The bird logged by name is now one tap away in the tally.
wait-for wren
tap wren
wait-for 1 species, 2 birds
# A pack pushed while the outing is open joins the tally when Fieldbook comes back.
companion fieldbook push scripts/fixtures/fieldbook/packs.v1 --sim
lifecycle background
lifecycle foreground
wait-for American Robin
expect-missing Type the first bird you see.
clean
shot nopack-pack-arrived
tap Back
wait-for 2 packs, 10 species.
expect Open outing: back garden
